 a target we  have not yet been hitting  away from the battlefield zelensky  thanked troops and handed out awards to  ukrainian fighters  aiming to boost the military spirits  i asked our correspondent matthias  bolinger if russian attacks are set to  increase because of western weapons  deliveries to ukraine  well that's how russia frames it they  are saying that they attack because of  western weapons deliveries they have  claimed that they hit  these tanks in kiev but  i think uh it's of course uh  the question of course western weapon  deliveries are a target for russia uh  that's very clear because the aim of  these attacks is to weaken ukraine's  infrastructure military infrastructure  but also civilian infrastructure russia  has hit by on  food  storages and and oil storages and  the question is would russia's  attacks decrease if the west didn't  deliver weapons and i don't think the  answer to that is very clear yeah good  question yes um tell me heavy fighting  continues in the dombass region can you  bring us up to date on that  yeah we're hearing that heavy fighting  is still underway in sierra donetsk  where the two armies are meeting each  other in the streets uh um we had heard  about some successes yesterday by the  ukrainians but it's very hard to confirm  anything except that both armies are  inside the city and we've seen heavy  attacks on other places on uh sweater  here's this is one of the  centers of the ukrainian  christian orthodoxy  where we've seen the church burning one  of a very historic church burning and  these attacks have continued today and  also only chance one of the places that  the president visited of course this  visit by the president um  uh is something that comes at a very  crucial at a very critical time for the  ukrainian army where it's under massive  attack and he took quite a risk to go  there  not only a risk but it's an important  message he's trying to get out there to  his people isn't it  of course it's a message of uh defiance  and and support and uh it is uh  of course the aim is to boost the morale  of the troops who are fighting there and  who are having huge losses  in this region  they are he has said it before that they  are losing up to 100 soldiers per day  that's a significant number for an army  and  a visit by him him taking this risk  personally is of course something um  that will have an impact on many of  these fighters dw correspondent matthias  burlinger thank you for the update  our military analyst frank ludwig joins  us from oxford  frank the uk sending its first  long-range missiles to ukraine despite  russia's threat the us is supplying a  rocket system are putin's threats of  more strikes just that threats  let's not forget ben that  the russians have already sent between  or fired between two and a half and  three thousand precision guided missiles  into ukraine over the last three months  so we can certainly expect some more of  that uh one thing i think that is worth  remembering is that we are required to  treat  for example this weekend five crew  cruise missiles into a european capital  as something that's vaguely russians  might be entitled to do but ukrainians  aren't entitled to strike back which  sadly is the reality of the situation  but to answer your question yes i think  we can um we can expect the russians to  try and cut the supplies or hamper the  supplies of western equipment  and to continue to do so  because frank what i'm getting at is um  another question i wanted to ask you  does russia have the capacity this far  into the war and considering all its  losses to increase its campaign  on the missile front i think western  analysts are pretty doubtful that russia  would want to expend too many more  missiles on the on these attacks more  widely though ben  it looks as if russia once again is  culminating in the latest phase of its  assault it has serious problems now with  manpower and and uh and i don't think  it's got the the s